  "articleBody": "Even if you enjoy tackling home improvements, some interior painting scenarios carry risks that call for professional help. Here are clear signs it is time to bring in an expert.\n\n- Persistent Moisture and Stains: Water marks, bubbling paint, or recurring damp spots mean moisture is trapped behind the drywall. Painting over them guarantees early failure.\n- Pre-1978 Construction: In homes built before 1978, disturbing painted surfaces can expose dangerous lead dust. Federal rules require certified firms using lead-safe containment and HEPA filtration.\n- Extensive Surface Damage: Widespread drywall cracking, popped nails, or peeling layers require full patching, skimming, and proper primers before repainting.\n- High Ceilings and Tough Access: Reaching multistory foyers or vaulted living rooms safely requires proper staging, ladders, and safety gear.\n- Incompatible Past Coatings: Glossy enamel or unknown older coatings require specialized bonding primers to avoid immediate peeling.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps: A skilled contractor diagnoses why old paint failed, seals stubborn stains with the right primer, and repairs damaged drywall before painting.\n\nIf your home shows any of these warning signs, connect with Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC by calling 303-505-0866 for a reliable assessment of your interior painting project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}